}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}]}, {"type": "DWS", "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 12, "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06re7pdf01.pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe8n4le03ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Paola:</span>  I've found an interesting article in a tech magazine about computers and information systems for our class. Shall I read it?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Christian:</span>  All right. But if you read it, can you read it slowly so that I can get it?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Paola:</span>  Okay. There's a lot of information in this magazine, so I'll just read some key parts.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Christian:</span>  Go ahead and do your best. If you don't make any mistakes while reading, I'll take some clear notes.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Paola:</span>  Fine, here I go. \u201cMany people, even those at a business environment, might think that a computer and an information system are almost the same simply because both process information, but this is far from certain. A computer is just a small piece within an information system that serves the purpose of transforming data into useful information. An information system, on the other hand, consists of a set of computers, robust databases for transactions and other operations, a few operating and application software packages, a lot of peripheral devices like printers, photocopiers, scanners, projectors, etc., and a large number of people resources as IT specialists and end users, and finally network resources that may include servers, wired/wireless routers, modems, data cables, switches and so on. The picture to the right illustrates this point.\u201d<br />", "image": "enpe8n4le03ob06re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Christian:</span> One moment, what picture? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Paola:</span> This one. Have a look at it. Hey, if you don't take any notes, how will we summarize all this info? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Christian:</span> Okay, give me a sec. That's it, ready. Excuse me Pao, let's have a short break, I must go to the bathroom.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Paola:</span>  No problem.  <br />", "image": "enpe8n4le03ob06re2img02.jpg", "time": "76000", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Christian:</span> I'm back. So, the difference is that an information system contains many computers as one of its main elements, but there are many more elements that an information system comprises.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\"> Paola:</span> Yeah, that's right.<br />", "image": "enpe8n4le03ob06re2img03.jpg", "time": "100000", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n4le03ob06re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}], "video_src": "enpe8n4le03ob06re5vsc01"}, "type": "video"}], "title": "", "id": 3, "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Computers and Information Systems "}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear/use to talk about information systems and computers."}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts. Design the data structure, starting from the conceptual model determined in the systems analysis, using database IT tools, according to regulation and established standards."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level Recognizes simple ideas on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "These are some types of conditional phrases in English. Some are possible; others are unlikely while others are impossible. <span class=\"strong\">The first conditional</span> deals with real conditions with a possible or imagined future consequence or result."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">The first conditional</span>  is composed by two clauses. One of them is the likely condition and the other clause is the imagined future consequence or result. It doesn't matter which clause you use first, but in case you begin with the conditional clause, a comma must be placed at the end of it before the second sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">If</span> we want to make good and informed decisions, we  <span class=\"strong\">will</span> have to invest in a solid information system.  <br/> -\tWe  <span class=\"strong\">will</span> have to invest in a solid information system  <span class=\"strong\">if</span> we want to make good and informed decisions.</span></br></br>As you can notice, in the second example the coma is not placed after the first clause because it starts with the possible future consequence."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Conditional clause</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The word   <span class=\"strong\">if</span> is widely used in the conditional clause. However, it is not the only way. Other words in replacement of <span class=\"strong\">if</span> are:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u2022   unless (if not)<br/>  \u2022   so long as <br/>  \u2022   as soon as (the moment)<br/>  \u2022   provided that (on the condition that / only if)  <br/> \u2022   whether (if) <br/> \u2022   after  <br/> \u2022   before   <br/>\u2022   when "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Unless </span>we finish this project on time, we <span class=\"strong\">may </span>likely <span class=\"strong\">assume </span>15% of additional expenses.  <br/><span class=\"strong\">After </span> having a comprehensive and approved plan, we <span class=\"strong\">will start</span> implementation of the new information system.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Whether</span> to help you succeed in the exam I have to prepare you for over a week, <span class=\"strong\">I'll do</span> it.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Grammar structure</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The grammatical structure for the first conditional is pretty simple."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If + subject + verb (present) + complement <span class=\"strong\">(Clause 1)</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + will/may/might/can + complement  <span class=\"strong\">(Clause 2)</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use   <span class=\"strong\">will</span> in the consequence or result clause to state that we believe the result will be definite or certain to happen. When we feel not so sure, we can use <span class=\"strong\">may/might</span> to state that the result is still possible but not definite. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">will</span> need to purchase two new laptops, a printer and a router <span class=\"strong\">if</span> these machines don't work. <br/><span class=\"strong\">If</span> after the test these second-hand machines work but not so well, we <span class=\"strong\">may</span> need to purchase a laptop, a printer or a router."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you read it, can you read it slowly so that I will get it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you don't make any mistakes while reading, I'll take some clear notes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hey, if you don't take any notes, how will we summarize all this info? "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Functional language, Make, Do, Have, Take"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Collocations</span> refer to the natural and regular use of some words that go together. People who have spoken the language all their lives recognize them as natural and identify their order easily."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Though there are many synonyms for a word we can use to express an idea and also to avoid redundancy, only some of them can go together and sound natural in a natural in any language. That is what linguists have called <span class=\"strong\">collocations</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now let's take a look at some common <span class=\"strong\">collocations</span> used in English for business and social contexts in connection with the verbs <span class=\"strong\">make, do, have and take</span> in the table below:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">do one's best, make the best of, have the best:</span> <span class=\"strong\">If you do your best</span>, it means you have acted correctly and that no-one can expect more from you. <span class=\"strong\">To make the best of a situation</span> means to take as much advantage as possible from a bad situation. See <span class=\"strong\">take advantage</span>. <span class=\"strong\">To have the best</span> is to be in possession of the best of something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">make a mistake:</span> to make an error."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">make notes, take notes: </span><span class=\"strong\">to make</span> or <span class=\"strong\">take notes</span> is to write the notes, usually to record on paper what someone is saying."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Take a look, have a look:</span> <span class=\"strong\">to take</span> or <span class=\"strong\">have a look at something</span> means to look at it (with purpose)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">do business, make business, take business, have business:</span> <span class=\"strong\">to do business</span> means to agree a commercial contract. <span class=\"strong\">To have business with someone</span> means to have matters to be settled with that person. <span class=\"strong\">To take business</span> is to deprive a competitor of a customer by acquiring that customer. <span class=\"strong\">To make business</span> is to create a business opportunity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">make an appointment, have an appointment:</span> <span class=\"strong\">to make an appointment</span> means to organize a meeting with other people. <span class=\"strong\">To have an appointment</span> means you are to participate in a meeting with other people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">make an argument, have an argument:</span> <span class=\"strong\">to have an argument with someone</span> means to argue with that person. <span class=\"strong\">To make an argument for something</span> means to present a logical argument in its favor."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">take action:</span> <span class=\"strong\">to take action</span> means to act positively and decisively to resolve a problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">take advantage, take advantage of, have an advantage:</span> <span class=\"strong\">to take advantage of something or someone</span> means to profit from the momentary situation of the person or thing. <span class=\"strong\">To have an advantage</span> means to be in a better position than someone else."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Go ahead and do your best."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you don't make any mistakes while reading, I'll take some clear notes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have a look at it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Excuse me Pao, let's have a short break, I must go to the bathroom."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "key part "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a very important element, piece, section or component of something."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There's a lot of information in this magazine, so I'll just read some key parts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "this is far from certain "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expression used to state that something is not as it has been affirmed or declared."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many people, even those at a business environment, might think that a computer and an information system are almost the same simply because both process information, but this is far from certain."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on the other hand "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "opposed to what was previously said or exposed."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An information system, on the other hand, consists of a set of computers, robust databases for transactions and other operations"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "give somebody a sec "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expression used to ask somebody to wait for a moment."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Okay, give me a sec. That's it, ready."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shall "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a question shall is used to make an offer, a suggestion or to ask for advice."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(modal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Shall I read it?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tech magazine "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a publication with specialized information about technology, technology applications and computers."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've found an interesting article in a tech magazine about computers and information systems for our class."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for information about the different resources in information system.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "identify positive and negative aspects of each one. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a comparative chart explaining the difference among the resources in information system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your comparative chart with your class and discuss about the topic. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search for information about different resources in information system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify positive and negative aspects of resources in information system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a comparative chart explaining the differences among the resources in information system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share information and discuss about resources in information system."}]}]}